# PCI on QEMU (M9; user/root/src/pci.rs; docs/design.md, "PCI on QEMU" and
# "Network scenarios"). Root carves the 2 MiB device frame over bus 0's
# ECAM out of device untyped and maps it uncached, scans q35 (the host
# bridge, the std VGA, the NIC and ICH9's LPC, AHCI and SMBus, printed for
# the record), finds virtio-net-pci at 00:02.0, sizes its BARs with
# decode off, checks its modern regions and MSI-X against them, carves
# their pages and the MSI-X table's, programs MSI-X entry 0 with
# IRQControl_GetMSI's message through the table page and reads it back
# (bus mastering stays off: no driver runs), maps the region pages and
# reads num_queues and the MAC without touching the device's status, prints the function's first 256 bytes as
# OVMF left them (user/pci/tests/q35-virtio-net.cfg), unmaps
# configuration space and the table, and prints the root CNode's slots.
cmdline: test=pci
exit: success
nic: virtio-net
expect: root: cmdline "test=pci"
expect: pci: ecam 0xe0000000, segment 0, buses 0-255
expect: pci: 00:02.0 1af4:1000 class 020000
expect: pci: virtio-net at 00:02.0: 1af4:1000, subsystem 1af4:0001;
expect: pci: virtio-net: common at BAR4+0x0, 4 KiB; notify at BAR4+0x3000, 4 KiB, notify_off_multiplier 4; device at BAR4+0x2000, 4 KiB
expect: pci: virtio-net: MSI-X 4 vectors, table at BAR1+0x0
expect: was masked (vector control 0x1); now IRQ 0: address 0xfee00000, data 0x30, unmasked, MSI-X enabled
expect: pci: virtio-net: 3 queues, MAC 52:54:00:12:34:56
expect: pci: cfg 00: f4 1a 00 10
expect: pci: configuration space and the MSI-X table unmapped
expect: TEST PASS
expect: DEBUG HALT 0 from TCB
forbid: TEST FAIL
